    {
      "id": "ESAT-SPECIMEN-BIOLOGY-Q1",
      "year": "specimen",
      "paper": "ESAT",
      "module": "biology",
      "question_number": 1,
      "question_text": "Which of the following describe(s) a role of mitosis?\n\n \n\n   1.  formation of gametes\n\n \n\n   2.  growth of cells\n\n \n\n   3.  repair of cells\n\n \n\n   4.  replacement of skin cells",
      "question_images": [],
      "screenshot": "esat_screenshots/biology/q01.png",
      "explanation_screenshot": "",
      "options": {
        "A": "1 only",
        "B": "2 only",
        "C": "3 only",
        "D": "4 only",
        "E": "1 and 2 only",
        "F": "3 and 4 only",
        "G": "1, 3 and 4 only",
        "H": "1, 2, 3 and 4"
      },
      "options_detailed": {
        "A": {
          "text": "1 only",
          "math_alt": [],
          "plain_text": "1 only"
        },
        "B": {
          "text": "2 only",
          "math_alt": [],
          "plain_text": "2 only"
        },
        "C": {
          "text": "3 only",
          "math_alt": [],
          "plain_text": "3 only"
        },
        "D": {
          "text": "4 only",
          "math_alt": [],
          "plain_text": "4 only"
        },
        "E": {
          "text": "1 and 2 only",
          "math_alt": [],
          "plain_text": "1 and 2 only"
        },
        "F": {
          "text": "3 and 4 only",
          "math_alt": [],
          "plain_text": "3 and 4 only"
        },
        "G": {
          "text": "1, 3 and 4 only",
          "math_alt": [],
          "plain_text": "1, 3 and 4 only"
        },
        "H": {
          "text": "1, 2, 3 and 4",
          "math_alt": [],
          "plain_text": "1, 2, 3 and 4"
        }
      },
      "correct_answer": "D",
      "correct_answer_raw": "",
      "correct_answer_plain": "4 only",
      "correct_answer_images": [],
      "explanation": "The answer is: 4 only.\nStatement 1 is incorrect as gamete formation occurs due to meiosis. Both statement 2 and statement 3 are also incorrect. However, they are common misconceptions held by students. Growth of an organism such as a human occurs by mitosis as the number of cells increases. The size of a cell does not increase due to mitosis. Mitosis results in the production of new cells which can be used to replace damaged cells in tissues such as muscles and organs such as skin. However, mitosis cannot repair cells, so statement 3 is incorrect.\nTherefore the only correct statement is statement 4 – replacement of skin cells.",
      "explanation_images": [],
      "extracted_at": "2026-07-05T00:07:47.807018",
      "options_latex": {
        "A": "1 only",
        "B": "2 only",
        "C": "3 only",
        "D": "4 only",
        "E": "1 and 2 only",
        "F": "3 and 4 only",
        "G": "1, 3 and 4 only",
        "H": "1, 2, 3 and 4"
      }
    },
    {
