    {
      "id": "ESAT-SPECIMEN-BIOLOGY-Q3",
      "year": "specimen",
      "paper": "ESAT",
      "module": "biology",
      "question_number": 3,
      "question_text": "Which of the four statements below about natural selection are correct?\n\n \n\n   1.  Competition occurs between individuals of the same species.\n\n \n\n   2.  Competition occurs between individuals of different species.\n\n \n\n   3.  Selection can lead to evolution.\n\n \n\n   4.  Selection can lead to extinction.",
      "question_images": [],
      "screenshot": "esat_screenshots/biology/q03.png",
      "explanation_screenshot": "",
      "options": {
        "A": "1 and 3 only",
        "B": "2 and 4 only",
        "C": "1, 2 and 4 only",
        "D": "1, 3 and 4 only",
        "E": "2, 3 and 4 only",
        "F": "1, 2, 3 and 4"
      },
      "options_detailed": {
        "A": {
          "text": "1 and 3 only",
          "math_alt": [],
          "plain_text": "1 and 3 only"
        },
        "B": {
          "text": "2 and 4 only",
          "math_alt": [],
          "plain_text": "2 and 4 only"
        },
        "C": {
          "text": "1, 2 and 4 only",
          "math_alt": [],
          "plain_text": "1, 2 and 4 only"
        },
        "D": {
          "text": "1, 3 and 4 only",
          "math_alt": [],
          "plain_text": "1, 3 and 4 only"
        },
        "E": {
          "text": "2, 3 and 4 only",
          "math_alt": [],
          "plain_text": "2, 3 and 4 only"
        },
        "F": {
          "text": "1, 2, 3 and 4",
          "math_alt": [],
          "plain_text": "1, 2, 3 and 4"
        }
      },
      "correct_answer": "F",
      "correct_answer_raw": "",
      "correct_answer_plain": "1, 2, 3 and 4.",
      "correct_answer_images": [],
      "explanation": "The answer is: 1, 2, 3 and 4.\nCompetition for limiting resources can occur both within a species (intraspecific – statement 1) and between species (interspecific – statement 2). Likewise, natural selection can lead to evolution due to individuals with advantageous adaptations being more likely to survive and pass on their alleles, thus passing on the advantageous adaptations to their offspring (statement 3). For a species that competes less well, natural selection may lead to extinction (statement 4). Therefore all four statements are correct.",
      "explanation_images": [],
      "extracted_at": "2026-07-05T00:08:12.878303",
      "options_latex": {
        "A": "1 and 3 only",
        "B": "2 and 4 only",
        "C": "1, 2 and 4 only",
        "D": "1, 3 and 4 only",
        "E": "2, 3 and 4 only",
        "F": "1, 2, 3 and 4"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "ESAT-SPECIMEN-BIOLOGY-Q4",
      "year": "specimen",
      "paper": "ESAT",
      "module": "biology",
      "question_number": 4,
      "question_text": "In rabbits, there are two alleles concerned with dark pigment in the fur:\n\n \n\n   • the dominant allele, B, for black colour\n\n \n\n   • the recessive allele, b, for brown colour\n\n \n\nTwo male black rabbits of unknown genotype each mated with a different female brown rabbit.\n\nWhat is the expected proportion of brown offspring if both male rabbits are heterozygous, and what is the expected proportion of brown offspring if only one male rabbit is heterozygous?",
      "question_images": [],
      "screenshot": "esat_screenshots/biology/q04.png",
      "explanation_screenshot": "",
      "options": {
        "A": "if both male rabbits heterozygous: 0.25, if only one male rabbit heterozygous: 0.5",
        "B": "if both male rabbits heterozygous: 0.25, if only one male rabbit heterozygous: 1",
        "C": "if both male rabbits heterozygous: 0.5, if only one male rabbit heterozygous: 0.25",
        "D": "if both male rabbits heterozygous: 0.5, if only one male rabbit heterozygous: 1",
        "E": "if both male rabbits heterozygous: 1, if only one male rabbit heterozygous: 0.25",
        "F": "if both male rabbits heterozygous: 1, if only one male rabbit heterozygous: 0.5"
      },
      "options_detailed": {
        "A": {
          "text": "if both male rabbits heterozygous: 0.25, if only one male rabbit heterozygous: 0.5",
          "math_alt": [],
          "plain_text": "if both male rabbits heterozygous: 0.25, if only one male rabbit heterozygous: 0.5"
        },
        "B": {
          "text": "if both male rabbits heterozygous: 0.25, if only one male rabbit heterozygous: 1",
          "math_alt": [],
          "plain_text": "if both male rabbits heterozygous: 0.25, if only one male rabbit heterozygous: 1"
        },
        "C": {
          "text": "if both male rabbits heterozygous: 0.5, if only one male rabbit heterozygous: 0.25",
          "math_alt": [],
          "plain_text": "if both male rabbits heterozygous: 0.5, if only one male rabbit heterozygous: 0.25"
        },
        "D": {
          "text": "if both male rabbits heterozygous: 0.5, if only one male rabbit heterozygous: 1",
          "math_alt": [],
          "plain_text": "if both male rabbits heterozygous: 0.5, if only one male rabbit heterozygous: 1"
        },
        "E": {
          "text": "if both male rabbits heterozygous: 1, if only one male rabbit heterozygous: 0.25",
          "math_alt": [],
          "plain_text": "if both male rabbits heterozygous: 1, if only one male rabbit heterozygous: 0.25"
        },
        "F": {
          "text": "if both male rabbits heterozygous: 1, if only one male rabbit heterozygous: 0.5",
          "math_alt": [],
          "plain_text": "if both male rabbits heterozygous: 1, if only one male rabbit heterozygous: 0.5"
        }
      },
      "correct_answer": "C",
      "correct_answer_raw": "",
      "correct_answer_plain": "C",
      "correct_answer_images": [],
      "explanation": "The answer is C.\nThe genotype of the female brown rabbits is bb.\nA homozygous black rabbit is BB. All of its offspring when crossed with a brown rabbit will be Bb and will be black.\nA heterozygous black rabbit is Bb. When crossed with a brown rabbit, the expected proportion of brown (bb) offspring is 0.5, with the other 0.5 being black (Bb).\nIf both the male rabbits are heterozygous, the expectation is that half the offspring from each mating will be brown, so the expected proportion of brown rabbits born from the two matings is 0.50.\nIf only one of the male rabbits is heterozygous, the other must be homozygous. The expected proportion of brown offspring of the heterozygous rabbit is 0.5, whilst all of the offspring of the homozygous rabbit will be black. The expected proportion of brown rabbits born from the two matings if only one of the male rabbits is heterozygous, is therefore 0.25.",
      "explanation_images": [],
      "extracted_at": "2026-07-05T00:08:25.393368",
      "options_latex": {
        "A": "if both male rabbits heterozygous: 0.25, if only one male rabbit heterozygous: 0.5",
        "B": "if both male rabbits heterozygous: 0.25, if only one male rabbit heterozygous: 1",
        "C": "if both male rabbits heterozygous: 0.5, if only one male rabbit heterozygous: 0.25",
        "D": "if both male rabbits heterozygous: 0.5, if only one male rabbit heterozygous: 1",
        "E": "if both male rabbits heterozygous: 1, if only one male rabbit heterozygous: 0.25",
        "F": "if both male rabbits heterozygous: 1, if only one male rabbit heterozygous: 0.5"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "ESAT-SPECIMEN-BIOLOGY-Q5",
      "year": "specimen",
      "paper": "ESAT",
      "module": "biology",
      "question_number": 5,
      "question_text": "A student carried out an experiment to investigate the effect of temperature on the rate of photosynthesis. All of the other variables were kept constant.\n\nThe graph shows the results obtained.\n\n \n\n \n\nThe student considered the graph and made the following conclusions.\n\n \n\n   1. Up to 22 °C temperature is limiting the rate of photosynthesis.\n\n \n\n   2. At temperatures higher than 22 °C not all of the enzymes work so the rate of photosynthesis drops. \n\n \n\n   3. As the temperature increases across the temperature range studied, the rate of photosynthesis increases due to increased kinetic energy. \n\n \n\nWhich of the student’s conclusions is/are correct?",
      "question_images": [],
      "screenshot": "esat_screenshots/biology/q05.png",
      "explanation_screenshot": "",
      "options": {
        "A": "none of them",
        "B": "1 only",
        "C": "2 only",
        "D": "3 only",
        "E": "1 and 2 only",
        "F": "1 and 3 only",
        "G": "2 and 3 only",
        "H": "1, 2 and 3"
      },
      "options_detailed": {
        "A": {
          "text": "none of them",
          "math_alt": [],
          "plain_text": "none of them"
        },
        "B": {
          "text": "1 only",
          "math_alt": [],
          "plain_text": "1 only"
        },
        "C": {
          "text": "2 only",
          "math_alt": [],
          "plain_text": "2 only"
        },
        "D": {
          "text": "3 only",
          "math_alt": [],
          "plain_text": "3 only"
        },
        "E": {
          "text": "1 and 2 only",
          "math_alt": [],
          "plain_text": "1 and 2 only"
        },
        "F": {
          "text": "1 and 3 only",
          "math_alt": [],
          "plain_text": "1 and 3 only"
        },
        "G": {
          "text": "2 and 3 only",
          "math_alt": [],
          "plain_text": "2 and 3 only"
        },
        "H": {
          "text": "1, 2 and 3",
          "math_alt": [],
          "plain_text": "1, 2 and 3"
        }
      },
      "correct_answer": "E",
      "correct_answer_raw": "",
      "correct_answer_plain": "1 and 2 only",
      "correct_answer_images": [],
      "explanation": "The answer is: 1 and 2 only.\nThe main factors affecting the rate of photosynthesis are light intensity, temperature and carbon dioxide concentration. Any change in the level of a factor will affect the rate of reaction and the process will be limited by the factor which is in the shortest supply.\nIn the case of temperature, the rate of reaction will increase until the optimum temperature for the enzymes controlling the reaction is reached, as long as the other factors are present in sufficient amounts. Therefore statement 1 is correct. After this point the enzymes start to become denatured and no longer work, so statement 2 is correct. An increase in temperature produces an increase in kinetic energy and, up to a temperature of 22 °C the rate of photosynthesis also increases. However temperature does not increase the rate across the whole of the range studied as after the optimum temperature has been reached, the rate of photosynthesis decreases. Therefore statement 3 is incorrect.",
      "explanation_images": [],
      "extracted_at": "2026-07-05T00:08:38.257996",
      "options_latex": {
        "A": "none of them",
        "B": "1 only",
        "C": "2 only",
        "D": "3 only",
        "E": "1 and 2 only",
        "F": "1 and 3 only",
        "G": "2 and 3 only",
        "H": "1, 2 and 3"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "ESAT-SPECIMEN-BIOLOGY-Q6",
      "year": "specimen",
      "paper": "ESAT",
      "module": "biology",
      "question_number": 6,
      "question_text": "The karyogram below is a photograph of the chromosomes taken from a single human cell.\n\n \n\nUsing the karyogram, which of the following statements is/are correct?\n\n \n\n   1. The karyogram shows no visible mutations.\n\n \n\n   2. The chromosomes are from a cell taken from a male.\n\n \n\n   3. The cell used could have been a white blood cell.\n\n \n\nImage used with permission of UW Cytogenetics/Wisconsin State Laboratory of Hygiene © Board of Regents of the University of Wisconsin System",
