    {
      "id": "ESAT-SPECIMEN-BIOLOGY-Q8",
      "year": "specimen",
      "paper": "ESAT",
      "module": "biology",
      "question_number": 8,
      "question_text": "The graph shows the mass of product produced over time for an enzyme-controlled reaction in two different conditions, X and Y. All other variables were kept constant.\n\n \n\n \n\nWhich of the following could be correct for this graph?\n\n \n\n   1. Condition X is a higher pH than condition Y.\n\n \n\n   2. Condition X has less substrate supplied than condition Y.\n\n \n\n   3. Condition X is a lower pH than condition Y.\n\n \n\n   4. Condition X has more substrate supplied than condition Y.",
      "question_images": [],
      "screenshot": "esat_screenshots/biology/q08.png",
      "explanation_screenshot": "",
      "options": {
        "A": "none of them",
        "B": "1 and 2 only",
        "C": "1 and 3 only",
        "D": "1 and 4 only",
        "E": "2 and 3 only",
        "F": "2 and 4 only",
        "G": "3 and 4 only",
        "H": "1, 2, 3 and 4"
      },
      "options_detailed": {
        "A": {
          "text": "none of them",
          "math_alt": [],
          "plain_text": "none of them"
