      "explanation": "The answer is row H.\nThe rate of gas production is given in the question as 2p mm3 per minute and the capillary diameter as 2 mm. The question also states that the experiment ran for 5 minutes so the total volume of gas collected was 5 × 2p = 10p mm3. To calculate the distance moved by the bubble of gas from this value you must use the equation pr2h, where r is the radius of the capillary tube and h is the distance moved by the gas bubble. The diameter of the capillary tube is 2 mm so the radius is 1 mm. This means that p × 12 × distance moved = 10p mm3, so the distance moved by the bubble is 10 mm.\nPhotosynthesis is an endothermic reaction so it must take in energy. In the case of energy this is in the form of light.\nIf the lamp was moved further away from the pondweed, it would decrease the light intensity shining on the plant. This would decrease the rate of photosynthesis, making the gas bubble move more slowly than the original experiment. As the gas is released from the plant it moves along the tube from left to right.\nThis makes the correct option H.",
